{
  "title": "Python Quest 2: For Loops",
  "levels": [
    {
      "title": "2.1 Square Dance",
      "instructions": "HQ: Four sides, all the same. Don't write it out four times. `for i in range(4):` repeats the lines indented under it. Add a `turn(90)` to the loop and set the distance.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(4):\n    step(100)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 300, "y": 150, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [
          { "x": 400, "y": 150 },
          { "x": 500, "y": 250 },
          { "x": 400, "y": 350 },
          { "x": 300, "y": 250 }
        ],
        "obstacles": [{ "x": 350, "y": 200, "w": 100, "h": 100 }]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.2 Staircase",
      "instructions": "HQ: A loop can repeat several lines. Each stair is 100 steps along and 75 steps up. Write one whole stair inside the loop, ending with Grep Fox facing right again, then repeat it 5 times.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(5):\n    step(100)\n    turn(-90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 150, "y": 450, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [{ "x": 650, "y": 75 }],
        "obstacles": [
          { "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 230, "h": 430 },
          { "x": 230, "y": 0, "w": 100, "h": 355 },
          { "x": 330, "y": 0, "w": 100, "h": 280 },
          { "x": 430, "y": 0, "w": 100, "h": 205 },
          { "x": 530, "y": 0, "w": 100, "h": 130 },
          { "x": 270, "y": 400, "w": 530, "h": 100 },
          { "x": 370, "y": 320, "w": 430, "h": 80 },
          { "x": 470, "y": 245, "w": 330, "h": 75 },
          { "x": 570, "y": 170, "w": 230, "h": 75 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.3 Long Stair",
      "instructions": "HQ: 12 stairs, each 60 steps along and 30 steps up. That's far too much to type out, but your loop doesn't care. Change one number.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(2):\n    step(60)\n    turn(-90)\n    step(30)\n    turn(90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 40, "y": 440, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [
          { "x": 220, "y": 350 },
          { "x": 400, "y": 260 },
          { "x": 580, "y": 170 },
          { "x": 760, "y": 80 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.4 Zigzag",
      "instructions": "HQ: Up 300, right 75, down 300, right 75, and the whole pattern happens 4 times. Put all of one pattern inside the loop, including the turns.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(4):\n    turn(-90)\n    step(300)\n    turn(90)\n    step(75)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 100, "y": 400, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [{ "x": 700, "y": 400 }],
        "obstacles": [
          { "x": 120, "y": 125, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 195, "y": 0, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 270, "y": 125, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 345, "y": 0, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 420, "y": 125, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 495, "y": 0, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 570, "y": 125, "w": 35, "h": 375 },
          { "x": 645, "y": 0, "w": 35, "h": 375 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.5 Spiral Out",
      "instructions": "HQ: Each side of this spiral is longer than the last. The loop variable `i` counts for you: `range(1, 3)` gives 1, then 2. Your code already walks `i * 60` steps, so make the range long enough for 5 sides.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(1, 3):\n    step(i * 60)\n    turn(90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 380, "y": 240, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [
          { "x": 440, "y": 360 },
          { "x": 260, "y": 360 },
          { "x": 260, "y": 120 },
          { "x": 560, "y": 120 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.6 Three Rooms",
      "instructions": "HQ: Three rooms in a row. Walk around each room with 4 sides of 100 steps, then `step(200)` to reach the next one. That's a loop inside a loop, so watch your indents.",
      "starterCode": "for side in range(4):\n    step(100)\n    turn(90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 150, "y": 200, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [
          { "x": 200, "y": 300 },
          { "x": 150, "y": 250 },
          { "x": 400, "y": 300 },
          { "x": 350, "y": 250 },
          { "x": 600, "y": 300 },
          { "x": 550, "y": 250 }
        ],
        "obstacles": [
          { "x": 175, "y": 225, "w": 50, "h": 50 },
          { "x": 375, "y": 225, "w": 50, "h": 50 },
          { "x": 575, "y": 225, "w": 50, "h": 50 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.7 Bug Parade",
      "instructions": "HQ: A parade of Sentry Bugs. You're safe when you stop halfway between two of them, so `step(200)` takes you from one safe spot to the next. Put a `wait` inside the loop and find the right number of seconds.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(3):\n    step(200)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 150, "y": 250, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [{ "x": 750, "y": 250 }],
        "guards": [
          { "route": [{ "x": 250, "y": 60 }, { "x": 250, "y": 440 }], "speed": 120 },
          { "route": [{ "x": 450, "y": 440 }, { "x": 450, "y": 60 }], "speed": 120 },
          { "route": [{ "x": 650, "y": 60 }, { "x": 650, "y": 440 }], "speed": 120 }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2.8 Boss: Fractal Garden",
      "instructions": "HQ: A growing spiral with a small room at each corner. Your code walks the spiral. At each corner, add a loop that walks a 50-step square, then turn. You'll need 4 corners in all.",
      "starterCode": "for i in range(1, 3):\n    step(i * 70)\n    turn(90)\n",
      "scene": {
        "start": { "x": 350, "y": 230, "angle": 0 },
        "chips": [
          { "x": 470, "y": 280 },
          { "x": 370, "y": 420 },
          { "x": 160, "y": 320 },
          { "x": 260, "y": 40 }
        ],
        "obstacles": [{ "x": 260, "y": 130, "w": 60, "h": 180 }]
      }
    }
  ]
}
